---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Walkthrough
seoTitle: "GTA 6 Walkthrough: All Story Missions, Step by Step"
description: "Every GTA 6 story mission in order across all five chapters, with a progress tracker, an option to hide mission names ahead of you, and step-by-step walkthroughs as they are written."
updated: 2026-11-23
faq:
  - q: "How many story missions are in GTA 6?"
    a: "About 90, spread over five chapters. The in-game story recap lists 93, and some guides count 91."
  - q: "How many chapters does GTA 6 have?"
    a: "Five. Each one earns a trophy when you finish it, the last one through the final mission."
  - q: "How long is the GTA 6 story?"
    a: "Roughly 50 to 80 hours for the main story, depending on how much you do on the side. Reported times range from just under 50 to around 80."
  - q: "Is there a point of no return in GTA 6?"
    a: "Yes, at the end of Chapter 1. After Recalibration the story runs straight through Tourist Trap, Home Sweet Home and Discharge Time with no free roam, and Jason is out of action for a long time. Make a separate manual save first and deposit your cash, since money in your pocket is lost and Jason's house in Key Lento is gone for good. Side jobs such as Kenton's dives come back later. There is a second one at the end of Chapter 4: once Sunset starts, the story runs on into Chapter 5 and the open world doesn't come back until most of Chapter 5 is done. The last two missions also run back to back, but after the credits you're put back just before the second-to-last one, so nothing in free roam is lost."
  - q: "How do you end Chapter 2 in GTA 6?"
    a: "Finish every other Chapter 2 story mission and save up $15,000, best kept in the BuckMe app. Checking Out then opens at the Starlet Motel. It ends the chapter and the motel stops being your home, so make a separate manual save and finish the Chapter 2 side jobs you want first."
  - q: "What is the final choice in GTA 6?"
    a: "At the very end of the last mission, The End of the Road, two options come up, and each leads to a different ending, and both earn the story trophy. There is no mission replay, so keep a manual save from before Protective Custody if you want to see both."
  - q: "Do you have to play the missions in this order?"
    a: "No. Within a chapter several missions can be done in a different order. This list follows the order of the in-game story recap."
---
{%- set missions = collections.missions %}
{%- set story = storyMissions %}
{%- set storyTotal = story.total or 0 %}
{%- set whoShort = { jason: "Jason", lucia: "Lucia", both: "Both" } %}
<header class="mast" style="--glow:var(--pink)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Story walkthrough</p>
    <h1>The Walkthrough</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Every story mission in order. Tick missions off as you finish them and this page keeps your place.</p>
    {%- if storyTotal or missions.length %}
    <div class="progress" data-progress="mission:" data-total="{{ storyTotal or missions.length }}">
      <div class="row"><span class="lab">Story progress</span><span class="pct"><span data-done>0</span> / {{ storyTotal or missions.length }} missions</span></div>
      <div class="bar"><i></i></div>
    </div>
    <div class="toolbar">
      <button type="button" class="toggle" data-pref="hideAhead" aria-pressed="false" data-on="Names of missions ahead are hidden" data-off="Hide names of missions ahead"><span class="sw" aria-hidden="true"></span><span data-label>Hide names of missions ahead</span></button>
    </div>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</header>

{%- if storyTotal %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="filters wt-filters" data-filter-group="story" role="group" aria-label="Show missions for">
      <span class="wt-filters-k">Show</span>
      <button type="button" class="fchip is-on" data-filter="*" aria-pressed="true">All missions</button>
      <button type="button" class="fchip" data-filter="jason" aria-pressed="false">Jason</button>
      <button type="button" class="fchip" data-filter="lucia" aria-pressed="false">Lucia</button>
      <button type="button" class="fchip" data-filter="todo" aria-pressed="false">Not done yet</button>
    </div>
    <p class="wt-filters-note">From Chapter 4 the story splits into Jason and Lucia strands that run side by side. Pick one to see only the missions you can play as that character. Missions played as both, and ones we can't place yet, stay in both lists.</p>
    <div data-filter-list="story">
    <div class="tip note wt-note"><span class="lab">Note</span><div class="tip-body"><p>The full mission list, in the order of the in-game story recap. It is first pass: we keep only missions that at least two independent lists agree on, and it is not yet checked in our own game. Missions with a written walkthrough are linked; the rest follow as we play. Turn on <b>Hide names of missions ahead</b> above if you want to avoid spoilers.</p></div></div>
    {%- for c in story.chapters %}
    <div class="chapter" id="chapter-{{ c.n }}" data-filter-parent>
      {%- set nGuides = c.missions | guidesIn(missions) %}
      <h2 class="chapter-h">Chapter {{ c.n }} <span>· {{ c.missions.length }} missions{% if nGuides %} · {% if nGuides == c.missions.length %}all guides written{% else %}{{ nGuides }} guide{% if nGuides != 1 %}s{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endif %}</span></h2>
      {%- if c.n == 5 %}<details class="spoiler"><summary><span class="sp-tag">Spoiler</span><span class="sp-what">Final chapter mission names</span><span class="sp-hint">Tap to reveal</span></summary><div class="sp-body">{% endif %}
      <ol class="mlist">
        {%- for m in c.missions %}
        {%- set ms = m.t | slugify %}
        {%- set mp = (missions | where("data.slug", ms))[0] %}
        {%- set who = (mp.data.protagonist if mp else m.who) %}
        <li class="mrow" data-track-row data-tags="{% if who == 'jason' %}jason{% elif who == 'lucia' %}lucia{% else %}jason lucia{% endif %}">
          <input class="cb" type="checkbox" id="m-{{ ms }}" data-track="mission:{{ ms }}" aria-label="Mark {{ m.t }} complete">
          <span class="mrow-no">{{ m.no | pad }}</span>
          {%- if mp %}
          <a class="mrow-title" href="{{ mp.url }}"><span class="t">{{ m.t }}</span></a>
          {%- else %}
          <span class="mrow-title"><span class="t">{{ m.t }}</span></span>
          {%- endif %}
          {%- if m.optional or mp or who %}
          <span class="mrow-tags">
            {%- if m.optional %}<span class="chip plain">Side job</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if mp and mp.data.missables and mp.data.missables.length %}<span class="flag">Missable</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if mp and mp.data.choices and mp.data.choices.length %}<a class="flag choice-flag" href="{{ mp.url }}#choices">Choice</a>{% endif %}
            {%- if who %}<span class="chip who {{ who }}">{{ whoShort[who] }}</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if mp %}<span class="chip ok dot">Guide</span>{% endif %}
          </span>
          {%- endif %}
        </li>
        {%- if m.warn %}
        <li class="mopens mwarn" data-follow><span class="mopens-k">{{ m.warn.k or "Point of no return" }}</span><a href="{{ m.warn.u }}">{{ m.warn.t }}</a></li>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if m.carry and m.carry.length %}
        <li class="mopens mcarry" data-follow><span class="mopens-k">Carries over</span>{% for o in m.carry %}{% if o.u %}<a href="{{ o.u }}">{{ o.t }}</a>{% else %}<span>{{ o.t }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</li>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if m.opens and m.opens.length %}
        <li class="mopens" data-follow><span class="mopens-k">Opens up</span>{% for o in m.opens %}{% if o.u %}<a href="{{ o.u }}">{{ o.t }}</a>{% else %}<span>{{ o.t }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</li>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
      {%- if c.n == 5 %}</div></details>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="nomatch" data-nomatch="story" hidden>Nothing left to show here.</p>
    <button class="reset" type="button" data-reset="mission:">Reset story progress</button>
  </div>
</section>
{%- elif not missions.length %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="empty">
      <p class="kicker">Opens at launch</p>
      <h2 class="sec-h sm">Mission guides start on November 19</h2>
      <p>Each walkthrough is written from the game itself, in story order, and published as soon as the mission has been played. Nothing here comes from leaks or guesses, so this list stays empty until the game is out.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/guides/launch-guide/">Read the launch guide</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- else %}
<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    {%- for group in missions | groupBy("data.chapter") %}
    <div class="chapter">
      <h2 class="chapter-h">{{ group.key or "Story missions" }}</h2>
      <ol class="mlist">
        {%- for m in group.items %}
        <li class="mrow" data-track-row>
          <input class="cb" type="checkbox" id="m-{{ m.data.slug }}" data-track="mission:{{ m.data.slug }}" aria-label="Mark {{ m.data.title }} complete">
          <span class="mrow-no">{{ m.data.order | pad }}</span>
          <a class="mrow-title" href="{{ m.url }}"><span class="t">{{ m.data.title }}</span></a>
          <span class="mrow-tags">
            {%- if m.data.missables and m.data.missables.length %}<span class="flag">Missable</span>{% endif %}
            {%- if m.data.protagonist %}<span class="chip who {{ m.data.protagonist }}">{{ whoShort[m.data.protagonist] }}</span>{% endif %}
          </span>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
    <button class="reset" type="button" data-reset="mission:">Reset story progress</button>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Reading these pages</p>
    <h2 class="sec-h">What the labels mean</h2>
    <div class="cards three">
      <div class="card"><span class="flag">Missable</span><h3>Things you can lose</h3><p>The mission has an item, trophy or choice you cannot return for. The page opens with a warning.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="chip ok dot">Verified</span><h3>Checked in the game</h3><p>The steps were replayed and confirmed on the game version shown. Pages not yet checked say so.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="chip who both">Both</span><h3>Who you play</h3><p>Shows whether the mission is Jason's, Lucia's or one you play as both.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- if faq %}
<section class="sec" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">FAQ</p>
    <h2 class="sec-h">Quick answers</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      {%- for q in faq %}
      <details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}><summary>{{ q.q }}</summary><div>{{ q.a | md | safe }}</div></details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ faq | faqld | safe }}</script>
{%- endif %}
